/**
 * VAPE's service icon, served at /favicon.ico as full-resolution 512x512 PNG
 * bytes embedded directly in the worker bundle.
 *
 * Why full resolution, not a traditional 16/32px favicon: x402scan's
 * discovery spec asks a registered origin to "serve a /favicon.ico at your
 * API root to display an icon" and x402scan renders that image as a large
 * profile-page avatar, not a browser tab icon. A previous fix here served a
 * 32x32 render (flattened to two-tone before downsampling to remove a
 * resample-induced gray halo around the glyph edges) — that solved the
 * aliasing artifact, but a 32px source blown up to avatar size is
 * unavoidably soft no matter how clean the pixels are; the "fuzzy logo"
 * complaint persisted after that fix because the resolution itself, not
 * just the anti-aliasing, was the ceiling. Serving the same 512x512 asset
 * used everywhere else (docs/assets/icon-512.png, and the Bazaar discovery
 * extension's iconUrl in src/index.ts) removes that ceiling entirely.
 *
 * Still inlined (not redirected/fetched) for the same reason as before: a
 * 302 to the GitHub Pages copy isn't reliably followed by directory
 * crawlers, and a runtime fetch would make an unpaid discovery route depend
 * on a third-party host being up. ~78KB base64 is negligible against a
 * Worker's script-size limit. Regenerate after changing the source:
 *   python3 -c "
 *   import base64
 *   print(base64.b64encode(open('docs/assets/icon-512.png','rb').read()).decode())"
 */
